I'm trying to remove an item in an array of arrays. I have tried using splice and pop but I'm not sure how to target the right element. My code is below. I am looking for a way to remove the item 'j' from the array.

const myArray = [['a', 'b', 'c'], ['d', 'e', 'f'], ['g', 'h', 'j']]

// expected output = [['a', 'b', 'c'], ['d', 'e', 'f'], ['g', 'h']]

I tried this code but it didn't work.

myArray[2].splice(2, 1, myArray[2].pop());

You need to splice the 2nd element of the outer array, not the inner array:
myArray.splice(2, 1);
// myArray = [['a', 'b', 'c'], ['d', 'e', 'f'], ['g', 'h']]
The 2nd argument is the number of elements to remove, the 3rd is the replacement (which you don't need).
For more info see the MDN documentation.

remove item in array of arrays
You can use Array#splice to remove the last item of the third array:

const myArray = [['a', 'b', 'c'], ['d', 'e', 'f'], ['g', 'h', 'j']];
myArray[2].splice(myArray[2].length - 1, 1);

console.log(myArray);
// [['a', 'b', 'c'], ['d', 'e', 'f'], ['g', 'h']]

