If the Internet had been invented during the Renaissance period, what would be the impact on the world?

A very large one, I think. A lot of people have speculated about this, and I'm sure there are many good books on the subject. Some of them are listed in the wikipedia article on the history of the Internet. I can't help you with the Renaissance part, but I think the Internet has had a huge impact on the world in general.

What are the differences between the Internet and the Renaissance period?

The Renaissance was a period in the history of Europe, and the Internet is a network that connects computers. They are two very different things.

What would be the impact of the Internet on the Renaissance?

It would have been a very different world. But that's the subject of many books and papers, not a forum question.

